      en: "Sénanque Abbey is a Cistercian monastery in the Vaucluse department in Provence. Founded in 1148, it is a fine example of Romanesque architecture. The church and cloisters are simple and harmonious. Monks still live here following the Rule of Saint Benedict. The abbey is surrounded by lavender fields used to produce lavender oil. It is a popular photographic subject.",
